---
description: BuddyBot multi-board safety and protocol rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Read docs/ARCHITECTURE.md and docs/PROTOCOL.md before editing firmware or comms.

One subsystem per change. Do not use old_firmware as current.

Never change 115200 baud, Mega D18/D19 ↔ Pico GP4/GP5, or the 5V divider on D18.
Never wire or "repurpose" Pico GP0/GP1.
Call bridgeLoop() only once per Pico loop.
MessageRouter.kt is the only Android parser for Mega lines.
Mega loop must stay non-blocking; keep 10s watchdog and 2s motor timeout.
Hazards override modes. No LLM on Mega/Pico.
Protocol changes update emitter + parser + docs/PROTOCOL.md together.
